Henne Brendel von Homburg, Schultheiß, Gerlach von Londorf, Hauptmann zu Frankfurt, Walter von Schwarzenberg, Jost im Steinhause, and Heinrich vom Rhein, Schöffen zu Frankfurt and all of them Freischöffen of the Holy Acht, vidimate under their seals, on the Monday after Palm Sunday 1439, the following document: Count Palatine Otto of the Rhine, guardian of the still underage Count Palatine Ludwig, declares that he has reconciled some citizens of Weißenburg and Walter Zeiß, through his councillors, namely Graf Emicho von Leiningen, the black Reinhard von Sickingen, Konrad von Rosenberg, (all?) Hofmeister, Schwicker von Sickingen, Vogt zu Bretten, Wiprecht von Helmstadt der Jüngere, Siegfried von Vennigen, all Ritter, Heinrich von Fleckenstein der Ältere and Heinrich von Berwangen, in their disputes over the claims that Walter makes against the citizens on grounds of honour and law. Walter receives safe conduct and security in order to obtain witnesses and documents from the city of Weißenburg for further court days before the Palatine councillors. - Seal of the issuer. - Given at Heidelberg on the Tuesday after the blessed martyrs Vitus and Modestus 1438 [= 1438 June 17];

Johann Zorn called von Eckenrich (?), Ritter, the master and the council of Strasbourg declare that before them Peter Butzroß, city scribe of Weißenburg, appeared in the name of the Weißenburg citizens Burkhard Freund, Heinrich Buschmann, Nikolaus Schuster (shoemaker), Nikolaus Hatten, Peter Heilwig, Kunz Heger, the shoemaker's, Peter durch den Wald, Nikolaus Falke and Keller, the baker's, and in the presence of Walter Zeiß presented to them a complaint by the Freigraf Hans von Menchenhusen in the land of Bilstein against the city of Weißenburg, directed against the judgment that Nikolaus Melbruge, current Ammeister, Nikolaus Schaulit and Jakob von Gabsheim, former Ammeister of the city of Strasbourg, delivered in disputes between the named Weißenburg citizens and Walter Zeiß. The said city scribe disputes Walter Zeiß's right to bring this matter before the Freigraf and the secret court, and demands that he be content with the judgment that was given. The Schöffen decide that the named arbitrators are to be induced to give a judgment once more in this matter, and that all other legal remedies are thereby to be excluded. The issuers seal with the city seal of Strasbourg. - Given on the Saturday before the Sunday Judica me domine 1439 [= 1439 March 21];

Florencze Wilckin, Freischöffe of the Holy Acht and citizen of Strasbourg, declares that the council of Strasbourg, in the disputes between some Weißenburg citizens and Walter Zeiß, on account of which the latter had sued them before the Westphalian courts, has established a new arbitration court with the knowledge and consent of both parties, which is to decide the disputes with binding legal effect. The arbitrators are the three named Strasbourg Ammeister. - Seal of the issuer. - Given on the Saturday immediately before the Sunday Judica me domine 1439 [= 1439 March 21].
